        <h1>My tutorial</h1>
        <h2>Software Development</h2>
        <p>
            This is a simple tutorial on software development.          
  software development is the process of designing, creating, testing, and maintaining software applications. It involves various stages such as requirements gathering, design,
   coding, testing, and deployment. The goal of software development is to create high-quality software that meets the needs of users and provides value to businesses.

        </p>
        <strong><h>Key Concepts:</h></strong>
        various stages of software development include:
        <ul>
            <li>Requirements Gathering: Understanding the needs and expectations of users and stakeholders.</li>
            <li>Design: Creating a blueprint for the software application, including architecture and user interface design.</li>
            <li>Coding: Writing the actual code to implement the software application.</li>
            <li>Testing: Verifying that the software works as intended and is free of bugs.</li>
            <li>Deployment: Releasing the software to users and making it available for use.</li>
         <strong><h>How to build a software application</h></strong>
            <li>Identify the problem or need that the software will address.</li>
            <li>Gather requirements from users and stakeholders to understand what features and functionality are needed.</li>
            <li>Design the software application, including its architecture, user interface, and database structure.</li>
            <li>Write the code to implement the software application, following best practices for coding and documentation.</li>
            <li>Test the software application to ensure it works as intended and is free of bugs.</li>
            <li>Deploy the software application to users and provide ongoing support and maintenance as needed.</li>
        </ul>
        <table border="1">
                <tr>
                    <th>Stage</th>
                    <th>Description</th>
                </tr>
